--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Other dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The desktop client pulls in further open-source libraries through Cargo and npm, and the released
installers are binaries that contain them. They are overwhelmingly MIT/Apache-2.0; the authoritative
list for a given build is its lockfile (tauri/src-tauri/Cargo.lock, tauri/package-lock.json), and
`cargo license` over that lockfile reproduces the licence set exactly. If you redistribute the
installers, carry that generated list with them.

Notable runtime components that are NOT bundled and must be installed separately by the user:
VB-CABLE (Windows) and BlackHole (macOS) as virtual microphones; on Linux the virtual microphone
is created at runtime through PulseAudio/PipeWire, which the client drives via `pactl`.
